node_modules
.env
# Broader than `.env` alone on purpose — `studios/vcut/.env.vstudio` (real-looking API keys, only
# ever untracked by luck, never by this file actually covering it) is exactly the shape of file this
# needs to catch: `.env.<anything>`. `.env.example` is the one file meant to be committed, so it's
# carved back out explicitly.
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
.claude/
.desktop/
# VStudio's project storage (repo-root fallback in dev — see packages/vstudio/README.md's
# "Where your files live"). Same category as .desktop/ above: local runtime data, not source.
.vstudio/
# Same as .vstudio/ above, under its post-rename name (VCUT_ROOT in studios/vcut/app/api/vcut/
# _lib/paths.ts) — local project/media storage, never source. Confirmed a real gap: this directory
# already held 374MB of local test project data, uncommitted only by luck (never actually excluded).
.vcut/
